cloud-hypervisor (52.0+ds1-0ubuntu2) stonking; urgency=medium

  * d/gen-copyright.py: fix upstream license to Apache-2.0 AND BSD-3-Clause
    (not OR) and add separate paragraphs for CC-BY-4.0 docs and
    Apache-2.0-only scripts/configs, matching .reuse/dep5 and regenerate
    d/copyright.
  * d/rules: exclude bundled C sources from vendor tarball via
    --exclude-crate-path for libssh2-sys#libssh2, openssl-src#openssl,
    zstd-sys#zstd, and libz-sys#src to avoid carrying extra license
    obligations (BSD-3-Clause, Zlib, etc.) from bundled C libraries.
  * d/rules: set ZSTD_SYS_USE_PKG_CONFIG=1 to link against system libzstd
    instead of compiling bundled sources.
  * d/control: add libzstd-dev to Build-Depends.
  * d/patches: drop
    0004-hypervisor-riscv64-drop-Irqchip-and-IrqRouting-cap-c.patch, the patch
    is not needed and was introduced by mistake due to a wrong use of QEMU TCG
    flags for RISC-V.

 -- Gauthier Jolly <gauthier.jolly@canonical.com>  Wed, 15 Jul 2026 10:22:40 +0200

cloud-hypervisor (52.0-0ubuntu1) stonking; urgency=medium

  * Initial release. (LP: #2158959)
  * New upstream release v52.0.
  * Vendor all Rust dependencies in a separate orig tarball.
  * Build for amd64, arm64, and riscv64.
  * d/p/0001-arch-vmm-fix-riscv64-build-gaps.patch: cherry-pick upstream
    commit 1e18716fbdc0 to fix riscv64 build.
  * d/p/0002-vmm-allow-riscv64-path-syscalls-in-seccomp-filters.patch:
    cherry-pick upstream commit 7d1321515cac to fix riscv64 seccomp filters.
  * d/p/0003-riscv64-clamp-AIA-SRCS-to-KVM-device-capacity.patch:
    cherry-pick upstream commits 085642dd423e and 649ca23345cc to clamp AIA
    interrupt sources to KVM device capacity, fixing EINVAL on riscv64
    platforms with smaller IMSIC capacity.
  * d/p/0004-hypervisor-riscv64-drop-Irqchip-and-IrqRouting-cap-c.patch:
    drop Cap::Irqchip and Cap::IrqRouting from riscv64 KVM capability
    checks; these capabilities are not exposed by RISC-V KVM, which uses
    AIA instead of the in-kernel irqchip, causing an unconditional panic
    at VM creation.

 -- Gauthier Jolly <gauthier.jolly@canonical.com>  Wed, 01 Jul 2026 11:00:17 +0200
